  "articleBody": "Installing pull-out cabinet shelves can be a game-changer for organization, but there are a few common mistakes that can turn it into a headache. Here's how to steer clear of them: \n\n1.  **Choosing the Wrong Size:** Don't just eyeball it! Measure the interior width, depth, and height of your cabinet precisely, accounting for any hinges or face frames. A shelf that's too wide or too shallow won't function properly.\n2.  **Mounting Slides Unevenly:** If your slides aren't perfectly level, your shelf won't glide smoothly. Always use a level to ensure both sides are installed at the exact same height.\n3.  **Ignoring Door Swing and Obstructions:** Make sure the shelf can fully extend without hitting the cabinet door or any internal elements like plumbing. Plan your hardware placement carefully.\n4.  **Overloading the Shelf:** Every pull-out shelf has a weight capacity. Piling on too much can damage the slides and make the shelf difficult to operate. Know your shelf's limits and stick to them.\n5.  **Not Considering Cabinet Framing:** If your cabinet has uneven or old framing, it can make a clean installation tricky. Sometimes you need to add shims or reinforcements. If you're facing any of these challenges, especially with a full kitchen remodel in areas like Aurora or Westminster, a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can ensure a flawless installation.",
